FINDING RAISED (led to a plan amendment, see Phase 1.5)
lib/email-parser/parse-statement.ts:51 instructs the extraction model to store
the NET amount disbursed to the owner in `amount`, explicitly "NOT the gross
rent income figure". lib/tax/rental-income.ts#actualRentForFy then reports that
column as gross rent. Six of the seven local rows arrived through that parser
and are not multiples of the $1,100 weekly rent. This understates assessable
rental income and contradicts the invariant this migration documents. Cause
confirmed in code; individual rows not yet audited. User approved folding the
fix into this track as Phase 1.5.

Also noted: statement fees are GST-inclusive ($220 + 10% = $242) while the
management_fee_pct estimate computes ex-GST. Residential rent is input-taxed,
so the GST-inclusive figure is the deductible one.
